implementationPlan.description:
docs/MCP_SERVER.md: the approval sections (CQ-F05 plus leftovers).

In `### Plan approval — expectedPlanRevision compare-and-swap`, and in `### moe.submit_plan` wherever it describes SPEED/TURBO auto-approval. Verify against src/tools/submitPlan.ts (armSpeedModeApproval, rearmSpeedModeApprovals) and state/taskStore.ts (updateTask, checkedApprovalRevision).

Token rules: replace the bullet 'Unchanged and still token-free: **SPEED/TURBO auto-approval** and the **`moe.set_task_status` relaxed-mode** approval…'. Only the relaxed set_task_status approval stays token-free, and it records no stamp. SPEED/TURBO now stamp (see below).

Durable authorization:
- Replace 'A number means a revision-checked human approval; …' with: a number is the revision an approval was bound to. That is either a token-checked human approval (PLAN_APPROVED) or a SPEED/TURBO automatic approval of the revision its plan submission committed (PLAN_AUTO_APPROVED). Keep the sentences about absent, null and no-backfill.
- Replace 'This records approval provenance only. Execution, claim and completion do not enforce it yet (CQ-F06–F08)…' with:
  - under an effective verified-local profile, step entry and completion require approvedPlanRevision === planRevision (link the moe.start_step, moe.complete_step and moe.complete_task sections);
  - claims never consult it;
  - the legacy/observe delivery policy is unchanged.

SPEED/TURBO facts (comment-b83aef8d, plus the worker clarification in comment-eee23c5e):
- TURBO stamps approvedPlanRevision = the submitted revision, in the same write as WORKING and planApprovedAt (inside the PLAN_SUBMITTED runExclusive).
- A SPEED timer approves only the revision it was armed for. After a plan, DoD or contract change, it WITHHOLDS:
  - no task write and no TASK activity;
  - one #general system message, which logs the usual non-task MESSAGE_CREATED activity, names both revisions and says 'Approve the current revision from the board, or reject the plan and resubmit it.';
  - the row stays AWAITING_APPROVAL with no live timer, and no timer is armed for the newer revision.
- Only PLAN_REVISION_MISMATCH withholds. Any other failure records the existing 'SPEED mode auto-approval failed' activity.
- The restart re-arm:
  - binds executionPolicySnapshot.planRevision (captured in the PLAN_SUBMITTED write);
  - for a legacy row with no snapshot, binds its current revision;
  - when the snapshot or revision is unreadable, records the failure activity and leaves that row unarmed;
  - never throws at daemon start;
  - at every restart, re-arms a withheld row (still bound to the older revision), which withholds again and posts one more notice.

Keep the CQ-F04/F04b text that is still true. Preserve all peer text.
